# direnv: enter the nix dev shell ONCE, then iterate with cargo/go/python
# directly. The dev shell only provides the toolchain + native libs (cuda,
# ctranslate2, whisper-cpp, onnxruntime, espeak-ng, libclang, ...); your code
# is built incrementally by cargo/go against the persistent target/ caches --
# nothing is rebuilt from scratch on each command.
#
# Default profile is `cuda` (assumes an NVIDIA GPU). To use the CPU shell
# instead, change the line below to:  use flake .#default
# Other profiles: .#python (torch/transformers), .#cuda-full, .#chat-only, ...
#
# First run:  direnv allow
# direnv re-evaluates ONLY when flake.nix / flake.lock change.
watch_file flake.nix flake.lock
use flake .#cuda
